# Solution for task old-hits
## Smarandoiu Elena-Andrada 315CA

After inspecting the code in Ghidra it's clear that the
programm generates a pseudo-random value by using the
function random() with the seed TIME(NULL);

By writing a similar C code and run it at the same time as
the executable old-hits we will get the same result:

'./a.out && ./old-hits'

In the function validate() the result is incremented with the
value 0x539, which is equal to 1337, so by adding the result 
of the random function with the value we will get the secret
number and the prize:

"Congrats! Here's your link: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=989-7xsRLR4"